{
  "semantics": {
    "attributes": {
      "final": {},
      "header": {}
    },
    "blocks": [
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The easiest way to receive a message asynchronously is to use the annotated listener endpoint infrastructure. In a nutshell, it lets you expose a method of a managed bean as a JMS listener endpoint. The following example shows how to use it:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "@Component\npublic class MyService {\n\n\t@JmsListener(destination = \"myDestination\")\n\tpublic void processOrder(String data) { ... }\n}"
              }
            ],
            "language": "java",
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The idea of the preceding example is that, whenever a message is available on the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "jakarta.jms.Destination"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "myDestination"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ", the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "processOrder"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " method is invoked accordingly (in this case, with the content of the JMS message, similar to what the "
              },
              {
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "MessageListenerAdapter"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "xref",
                "target": "integration/jms/receiving.html#jms-receiving-async-message-listener-adapter"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " provides)."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The annotated endpoint infrastructure creates a message listener container behind the scenes for each annotated method, by using a "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "JmsListenerContainerFactory"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ". Such a container is not registered against the application context but can be easily located for management purposes by using the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "JmsListenerEndpointRegistry"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " bean."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "admonition",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "@JmsListener"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " is a repeatable annotation on Java 8, so you can associate several JMS destinations with the same method by adding additional "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "@JmsListener"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " declarations to it."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null,
            "type": "tip"
          }
        ],
        "context": "preamble",
        "id": null,
        "outline": null,
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "To enable support for "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "@JmsListener"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " annotations, you can add "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "@EnableJms"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " to one of your "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "@Configuration"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " classes, as the following example shows:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "include-code::./JmsConfiguration[tag=snippet,indent=0]"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "By default, the infrastructure looks for a bean named "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "jmsListenerContainerFactory"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " as the source for the factory to use to create message listener containers. In this case (and ignoring the JMS infrastructure setup), you can invoke the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "processOrder"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " method with a core pool size of three threads and a maximum pool size of ten threads."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "You can customize the listener container factory to use for each annotation or you can configure an explicit default by implementing the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "JmsListenerConfigurer"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " interface. The default is required only if at least one endpoint is registered without a specific container factory. See the javadoc of classes that implement "
              },
              {
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "JmsListenerConfigurer"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "link",
                "target": "https://docs.spring.io/spring-framework/docs/6.2.0/javadoc-api/org/springframework/jms/annotation/JmsListenerConfigurer.html"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " for details and examples."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "section",
        "id": "jms-annotated-support",
        "level": 1,
        "roles": [],
        "title": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Enable Listener Endpoint Annotations"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "JmsListenerEndpoint"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " provides a model of a JMS endpoint and is responsible for configuring the container for that model. The infrastructure lets you programmatically configure endpoints in addition to the ones that are detected by the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "JmsListener"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " annotation. The following example shows how to do so:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "@Configuration\n@EnableJms\npublic class AppConfig implements JmsListenerConfigurer {\n\n\t@Override\n\tpublic void configureJmsListeners(JmsListenerEndpointRegistrar registrar) {\n\t\tSimpleJmsListenerEndpoint endpoint = new SimpleJmsListenerEndpoint();\n\t\tendpoint.setId(\"myJmsEndpoint\");\n\t\tendpoint.setDestination(\"anotherQueue\");\n\t\tendpoint.setMessageListener(message -> {\n\t\t\t// processing\n\t\t});\n\t\tregistrar.registerEndpoint(endpoint);\n\t}\n}"
              }
            ],
            "language": "java",
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "In the preceding example, we used "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "SimpleJmsListenerEndpoint"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ", which provides the actual "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "MessageListener"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " to invoke. However, you could also build your own endpoint variant to describe a custom invocation mechanism."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Note that you could skip the use of "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "@JmsListener"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " altogether and programmatically register only your endpoints through "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "JmsListenerConfigurer"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "section",
        "id": "jms-annotated-programmatic-registration",
        "level": 1,
        "roles": [],
        "title": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Programmatic Endpoint Registration"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "So far, we have been injecting a simple "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "String"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " in our endpoint, but it can actually have a very flexible method signature. In the following example, we rewrite it to inject the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "Order"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " with a custom header:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "@Component\npublic class MyService {\n\n\t@JmsListener(destination = \"myDestination\")\n\tpublic void processOrder(Order order, @Header(\"order_type\") String orderType) {\n\t\t...\n\t}\n}"
              }
            ],
            "language": "java",
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The main elements you can inject in JMS listener endpoints are as follows:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "ulist",
            "id": null,
            "items": [
              {
                "blocks": [],
                "checkbox": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "The raw "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "jakarta.jms.Message"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " or any of its subclasses (provided that it matches the incoming message type)."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "blocks": [],
                "checkbox": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "The "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "jakarta.jms.Session"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " for optional access to the native JMS API (for example, for sending a custom reply)."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "blocks": [],
                "checkbox": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "The "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "org.springframework.messaging.Message"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " that represents the incoming JMS message. Note that this message holds both the custom and the standard headers (as defined by "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "JmsHeaders"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": ")."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "blocks": [],
                "checkbox": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "@Header"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "-annotated method arguments to extract a specific header value, including standard JMS headers."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "blocks": [],
                "checkbox": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "A "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "@Headers"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "-annotated argument that must also be assignable to "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "java.util.Map"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " for getting access to all headers."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "blocks": [],
                "checkbox": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "A non-annotated element that is not one of the supported types ("
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "Message"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " or "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "Session"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": ") is considered to be the payload. You can make that explicit by annotating the parameter with "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "@Payload"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": ". You can also turn on validation by adding an extra "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "@Valid"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "style": null,
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The ability to inject Spring’s "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "Message"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " abstraction is particularly useful to benefit from all the information stored in the transport-specific message without relying on transport-specific API. The following example shows how to do so:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "@JmsListener(destination = \"myDestination\")\npublic void processOrder(Message<Order> order) { ... }"
              }
            ],
            "language": "java",
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Handling of method arguments is provided by "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "DefaultMessageHandlerMethodFactory"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ", which you can further customize to support additional method arguments. You can customize the conversion and validation support there as well."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "For instance, if we want to make sure our "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "Order"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " is valid before processing it, we can annotate the payload with "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "@Valid"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " and configure the necessary validator, as the following example shows:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "@Configuration\n@EnableJms\npublic class AppConfig implements JmsListenerConfigurer {\n\n\t@Override\n\tpublic void configureJmsListeners(JmsListenerEndpointRegistrar registrar) {\n\t\tregistrar.setMessageHandlerMethodFactory(myJmsHandlerMethodFactory());\n\t}\n\n\t@Bean\n\tpublic DefaultMessageHandlerMethodFactory myHandlerMethodFactory() {\n\t\tDefaultMessageHandlerMethodFactory factory = new DefaultMessageHandlerMethodFactory();\n\t\tfactory.setValidator(myValidator());\n\t\treturn factory;\n\t}\n}"
              }
            ],
            "language": "java",
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "section",
        "id": "jms-annotated-method-signature",
        "level": 1,
        "roles": [],
        "title": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Annotated Endpoint Method Signature"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The existing support in "
              },
              {
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "MessageListenerAdapter"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "xref",
                "target": "integration/jms/receiving.html#jms-receiving-async-message-listener-adapter"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " already lets your method have a non-"
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "void"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " return type. When that is the case, the result of the invocation is encapsulated in a "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "jakarta.jms.Message"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ", sent either in the destination specified in the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "JMSReplyTo"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " header of the original message or in the default destination configured on the listener. You can now set that default destination by using the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "@SendTo"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " annotation of the messaging abstraction."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Assuming that our "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "processOrder"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " method should now return an "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "OrderStatus"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ", we can write it to automatically send a response, as the following example shows:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "@JmsListener(destination = \"myDestination\")\n@SendTo(\"status\")\npublic OrderStatus processOrder(Order order) {\n\t// order processing\n\treturn status;\n}"
              }
            ],
            "language": "java",
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "admonition",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "If you have several "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "@JmsListener"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "-annotated methods, you can also place the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "@SendTo"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " annotation at the class level to share a default reply destination."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null,
            "type": "tip"
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "If you need to set additional headers in a transport-independent manner, you can return a "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "Message"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " instead, with a method similar to the following:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "@JmsListener(destination = \"myDestination\")\n@SendTo(\"status\")\npublic Message<OrderStatus> processOrder(Order order) {\n\t// order processing\n\treturn MessageBuilder\n\t\t\t.withPayload(status)\n\t\t\t.setHeader(\"code\", 1234)\n\t\t\t.build();\n}"
              }
            ],
            "language": "java",
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "If you need to compute the response destination at runtime, you can encapsulate your response in a "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "JmsResponse"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " instance that also provides the destination to use at runtime. We can rewrite the previous example as follows:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "@JmsListener(destination = \"myDestination\")\npublic JmsResponse<Message<OrderStatus>> processOrder(Order order) {\n\t// order processing\n\tMessage<OrderStatus> response = MessageBuilder\n\t\t\t.withPayload(status)\n\t\t\t.setHeader(\"code\", 1234)\n\t\t\t.build();\n\treturn JmsResponse.forQueue(response, \"status\");\n}"
              }
            ],
            "language": "java",
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Finally, if you need to specify some QoS values for the response such as the priority or the time to live, you can configure the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "JmsListenerContainerFactory"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " accordingly, as the following example shows:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "@Configuration\n@EnableJms\npublic class AppConfig {\n\n\t@Bean\n\tpublic DefaultJmsListenerContainerFactory jmsListenerContainerFactory() {\n\t\tDefaultJmsListenerContainerFactory factory = new DefaultJmsListenerContainerFactory();\n\t\tfactory.setConnectionFactory(connectionFactory());\n\t\tQosSettings replyQosSettings = new QosSettings();\n\t\treplyQosSettings.setPriority(2);\n\t\treplyQosSettings.setTimeToLive(10000);\n\t\tfactory.setReplyQosSettings(replyQosSettings);\n\t\treturn factory;\n\t}\n}"
              }
            ],
            "language": "java",
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "section",
        "id": "jms-annotated-response",
        "level": 1,
        "roles": [],
        "title": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Response Management"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "outline": null,
    "title": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "value": "Annotation-driven Listener Endpoints"
      }
    ]
  }
}
